WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.990
Travel back four billion years,

2
00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:04.770
and you could not breathe on Earth.

3
00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:06.570
Volcanoes are pouring out gases,

4
00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:11.870
and the air is full of carbon
dioxide, with little or no oxygen.

5
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.310
Now look at the air around you today.

6
00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:18.250
About four-fifths is nitrogen,
about one-fifth is oxygen,

7
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:21.970
and carbon dioxide is just
a small part of the rest.

8
00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:24.670
So where did all that
carbon dioxide go?

9
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:26.470
And what made the oxygen?

10
00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:29.890
In this mission, you'll see
what the volcanoes released,

11
00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:31.710
how the young oceans formed,

12
00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:34.690
and how algae and then
plants changed the air.

13
00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:38.150
You'll also learn what
today's air is made of.

14
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:42.330
Your mission: explain how
Earth's air was transformed.
